NV_PK(12,{"from the lawn you can see a row of stone tablets below the sea god temple in the qing dynasty this red roofed pavilion was built on the old dutch base":"","look up at the sea god temple it has red tiles two layers of roof and corners that curve up high it is the front pavilion and wenchang pavilion stands behind it":"","each stone tablet stands on the back of a bixi beside a koi pond a bixi looks like a turtle it is said to be one of the dragon's nine sons and it loves carrying heavy things":"","the two words at the top mean written by the emperor and dragons curl around them after the lin shuangwen uprising emperor qianlong wrote these texts in 1788":"","a statue in the garden shows koxinga and the dutch making peace in 1661 the dutch gave up this fort":"","chinese style halls were built on the dutch base in the qing dynasty":"","the qing emperors were manchu so the texts are in chinese and manchu":"","dutch bricks koxinga's office qing pavilions and a japanese hospital all on one hill":"","from a dutch fort to koxinga's office qing pavilions imperial tablets and a japanese hospital four hundred years on one site":"","built on the old base in the late qing with red tiles and upturned eaves":"","one site shows the dutch zheng qing and japanese eras together":""});